          "id": "2844173a5b30fc4345076e839d78861106da263a",
          "message": "docs(research): bridge the FO/LLM fluency gap — facade+hide over a hidden rich-FO backbone (sq-8dkyo) [OPUS-4.8] (#1112)\n\nSynthesise four research streams (teach / facade / hide / coverage) into\nresearch/fo-llm-bridge.md. Reframes the maintainer's 3 directions as a\nspectrum of how-much-ontology-to-expose; honest verdict: evidence favours\n(2) facade + (3) hide over (1) teach-as-primary (FO-KM Metric 1 + Köhler &\nNeuhaus). Recommends rich FO confined to the reasoner/validator, a fluent\nschema.org/gist facade on the read-path, vector V() concept-resolution to\nhide URIs, and a YAML-LD-like structured authoring form that deterministically\ncompiles to FO triples on the write-path. Broadens the benchmark (add gist +\nBFO across the size axis) with pre-registered kill-criteria; backbone value is\nEC2-deferred (sq-p5ro8) and currently sign-unstable, so the design is kept\nfalsifiable. Corrects brief premises: bench/fo-km harness is in OPEN PRs\n(#1107/#1108) not on main; sparq-terse is MERGED (#1088); JSON-LD compaction\nis shipped (sq-ixc3.4 CLOSED, #950).\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-22T14:45:23Z",
